--
-- Tests for bc-interpretation-time.l4: how a period of days, weeks, months or years is counted
-- (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, ss 25 to 25.4).
--
-- Every expected value below was decided by reading the section and counting by hand, and was
-- written down before this file was first run. A failing assertion is a finding about the code
-- or about the reading, never a reason to edit the expected value.
--
-- Reading of the counting rule, applied throughout (NOTES, fork F-count):
--   * a period from or after a reference day does not include the reference day: counting starts
--     "from and including the day after the reference day" (s 25.2(2)(a));
--   * the last day of the period is inside it;
--   * for months and years the period ends on "the date numerically corresponding to the
--     reference day" in the month (year) in which it ends (ss 25.3(1)(a), 25.4(1)(a)).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-time`

GIVETH A `Position of the reference day`
`ref before the period` MEANS `The reference day is before the period`

GIVETH A `Position of the reference day`
`ref after the period` MEANS `The reference day is after the period`

§ `Days and weeks, s 25.2`

-- One day from 1 January: counting forward from and including 2 January, day 1 is 2 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2

-- Worked case: thirty days from 2026-01-01. 2 January is day 1, so day 30 is 31 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

-- The day after the last day is outside, and so is the reference day itself.
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 31) (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))

-- A week is 7 consecutive days (s 25.2(1)).
#ASSERT `s 25.2(1) the number of days in a week` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of weeks counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 8
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of weeks counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15

-- Across the end of a month: 15 February 2026 plus 13 days is 28 February; 17 more is 17 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 2 15) 30 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 17

-- Across the end of a year.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2025 12 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1

-- Across a leap day: 29 February 2024 is day 1, 1 March is day 2.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2024 2 28) 1 EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2024 2 28) 2 EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1

-- 365 days from 1 March 2024 reaches 1 March 2025 (the leap day is before the start); 366 days
-- from 1 March 2023 reaches 1 March 2024 (the leap day is inside).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2024 3 1) 365 EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2023 3 1) 366 EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1

-- Reference day after the period: counting backward from and including the day before it
-- (s 25.2(2)(b)). One day before 10 January: day 1 is 9 January.
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 1 9
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` 7 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 1 3
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of weeks` (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 1 3
-- Ten days before 5 January 2026: 4 Jan is day 1, 1 Jan day 4, 31 Dec day 5, 26 Dec day 10.
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2026 1 5) `ref after the period` 10 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2025 12 26

-- "Clear" days or weeks, "at least" or "not less than": one day later when the reference day is
-- before the period, one day earlier when it is after (s 25.2(3)).
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 1 3
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` 30 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of weeks` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 1 9
#ASSERT `s 25.2 beginning or end of a period of days` (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` 7 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2

§ `Months, s 25.3`

-- The date numerically corresponding to the reference day, in the month in which the period ends.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 15) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1

-- Worked case: one month from 2025-01-31. "31 February" does not occur, so the period ends on the
-- last day of that month (s 25.3(3)).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 1 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

-- A month that lacks the start day's number, in a leap year and not.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2024 1 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 1 30) 1 EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2024 1 30) 1 EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2024 1 29) 1 EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 1 29) 1 EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 3 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 5 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2025 6 30
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 4 30) 1 EQUALS YMD 2025 5 30

-- The end falls in another calendar year; several months; a start on the 31st.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 12 15) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 12 31) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 3 15) 12 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 12 15) 13 EQUALS YMD 2027 1 15
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 8 31) 6 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2025 7 31) 6 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

-- Reference day after the period: going backward to the date numerically corresponding to it
-- (s 25.3(1)(b)); a date that does not occur gives the last day of the month (s 25.3(3)).
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 3 15) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 2 15
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2025 3 31) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2024 3 31) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 1 15) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2025 12 15
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 1 31) `ref after the period` 2 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2025 11 30

-- "Clear" months: one day later (forward) or earlier (backward) than the date under s 25.3(1).
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 1 15) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 2 16
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2024 1 29) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 1 28) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 3 15) `ref after the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 2 14
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 3 1) `ref after the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref after the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2025 11 30

-- "Clear" months where the corresponding date does not occur: the text does not say whether the
-- one-day shift comes before or after the last-day-of-the-month rule, and the two readings give
-- different days (NOTES, fork F-clear). The module refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2025 1 31) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 25.3 does not say how to shift a clear month by a day when the day numerically corresponding to the reference day does not occur"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2025 1 29) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2025 3 31) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.3 beginning or end of a period of months` (YMD 2025 3 31) `ref after the period` 1 TRUE

§ `Years, s 25.4`

-- Worked cases: the date numerically corresponding to the reference day, in the same month.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2025 7 16) 3 EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2025 1 15) 5 EQUALS YMD 2030 1 15
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2025 9 1) 5 EQUALS YMD 2030 9 1
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2024 2 28) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

-- Worked case: one year from 2024-02-29. 29 February 2025 does not occur, so 28 February (s 25.4(3)).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2024 2 29) 1 EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28

-- Starts on 29 February: the leap day exists again after four years, and not after two or three.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2024 2 29) 4 EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2024 2 29) 8 EQUALS YMD 2032 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2024 2 29) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2024 2 29) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28

-- 28 February is never moved, even when the year in which the period ends has a 29 February.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2023 2 28) 1 EQUALS YMD 2024 2 28

-- A start at the end or the beginning of a year.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2025 12 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1

-- Reference day after the period: going backward (s 25.4(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2026 7 16) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2025 2 28) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2024 2 28
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref after the period` 1 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2023 2 28
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref after the period` 4 FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 2 29

-- "Clear" years: one day later (forward) or earlier (backward) (s 25.4(2)).
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2025 7 16) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2026 7 17
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2023 2 28) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2024 2 28) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2025 3 1
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref before the period` 4 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2028 3 1
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2025 12 31) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2027 1 1
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2026 7 16) `ref after the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2025 7 15
#ASSERT `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref after the period` 1 TRUE EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31

-- "Clear" years from 29 February into a year that has none: the text does not say whether the
-- one-day shift comes before or after the 28 February rule (NOTES, fork F-clear).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref before the period` 1 TRUE
        BECAUSE "s 25.4 does not say how to shift a clear year by a day when the reference day is 29 February and the year has none"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25.4 beginning or end of a period of years` (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref after the period` 1 TRUE

§ `Counting any period: the dispatcher and the four named functions`

#ASSERT `the beginning or end of a period` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days,   `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the beginning or end of a period` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Weeks,  `how many` IS 2,  `clear` IS FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 15
#ASSERT `the beginning or end of a period` (YMD 2025 1 31) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1,  `clear` IS FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the beginning or end of a period` (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Years,  `how many` IS 1,  `clear` IS FALSE) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the beginning or end of a period` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days,   `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT `the beginning or end of a period` (YMD 2026 3 15) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1,  `clear` IS TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 14

§ `Where a period lies, and whether a day is inside it`

-- Days: 30 days from 1 January 2026 occupy 2 January to 31 January.
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
#ASSERT (`the span of days of a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE))'s `last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

-- The first day inside and the day before it outside; the last day inside and the day after outside.
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 2) (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 1) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 30, `clear` IS FALSE)

-- One week before 10 January 2026 occupies 3 January to 9 January.
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 3) (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Weeks, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 9) (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Weeks, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 2) (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Weeks, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 10) `ref after the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Weeks, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))

-- One day: the period is the single day after the reference day.
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 5 11) (YMD 2026 5 10) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 5 10) (YMD 2026 5 10) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2026 5 12) (YMD 2026 5 10) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Days, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))

-- One month from 2025-01-31 occupies 1 February to 28 February (fork F-month: the period starts
-- the day after the reference day).
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2025 2 1) (YMD 2025 1 31) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2025 2 28) (YMD 2025 1 31) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 1 31) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2025 1 31) (YMD 2025 1 31) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))

-- One year from 2024-02-29 occupies 1 March 2024 to 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2024 3 1) (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Years, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2025 2 28) (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Years, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Years, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 29) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Years, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS FALSE))

-- A clear period that the text cannot count has no span: the question is refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `a day falls inside a period counted from a reference day` (YMD 2025 2 28) (YMD 2025 1 31) `ref before the period` (`Period of time` WITH `unit` IS Months, `how many` IS 1, `clear` IS TRUE)

§ `A count that is not one or more whole units`

-- ss 25.2(2), 25.3(1) and 25.4(1) speak of "one day or consecutive days", "one month or
-- consecutive months", "one year or consecutive years". A count of nought, a negative count or a
-- fraction is not such a period, and the text says nothing about it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 0
        BECAUSE "ss 25.2 to 25.4 count a whole number of one or more days, weeks, months or years"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) -1
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1.5
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of weeks counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of weeks counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 0.5
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) -2
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) 2.5
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of years counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1.5
-- One is the smallest count, and it is accepted.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of days counted from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of months counted after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
